{
"title": "3. Factorisation of Polynomials",
"tests": [
{"q": [
{"t": "Factorise: x² − 16", "o": ["(x + 4)(x − 4)", "(x − 4)²", "(x + 8)(x − 2)", "(x − 16)(x + 1)"], "e": "A difference of squares: a² − b² = (a + b)(a − b)."},
{"t": "Factorise: x² + 7x + 12", "o": ["(x + 3)(x + 4)", "(x + 2)(x + 6)", "(x + 1)(x + 12)", "(x − 3)(x − 4)"], "e": "Two numbers with product 12 and sum 7: 3 and 4."},
{"t": "(a + b)³ equals:", "o": ["a³ + 3a²b + 3ab² + b³", "a³ + b³", "a³ + 3ab + b³", "a³ + a²b + ab² + b³"], "e": "(a + b)(a + b)² — multiplying out gives two extra groups, 3a²b and 3ab²."},
{"t": "Factorise: 9x² − 1", "o": ["(3x + 1)(3x − 1)", "(3x − 1)²", "(9x + 1)(x − 1)", "(9x − 1)(x + 1)"], "e": "(3x)² − 1²."},
{"t": "Factorise: x² − 5x + 6", "o": ["(x − 2)(x − 3)", "(x + 2)(x + 3)", "(x − 1)(x − 6)", "(x − 6)(x + 1)"], "e": "Product +6 and sum −5: −2 and −3."},
{"t": "Factorise: 3x² + 6x", "o": ["3x(x + 2)", "3(x² + 6x)", "x(3x + 2)", "3x(x + 6)"], "e": "Take out the HCF, 3x."},
{"t": "a³ + b³ equals:", "o": ["(a + b)(a² − ab + b²)", "(a + b)(a² + ab + b²)", "(a + b)³", "(a − b)(a² + ab + b²)"], "e": "Check by multiplying out: the middle terms cancel, leaving a³ + b³. Note the minus in the second bracket."},
{"t": "Expand: (x + 2)²", "o": ["x² + 4x + 4", "x² + 4", "x² + 2x + 4", "x² + 4x + 2"], "e": "a² + 2ab + b² with a = x, b = 2."},
{"t": "Factorise: 4x² + 12x + 9", "o": ["(2x + 3)²", "(4x + 3)(x + 3)", "(2x + 9)(2x + 1)", "(2x − 3)²"], "e": "(2x)² + 2(2x)(3) + 3²."},
{"t": "a² − b² equals:", "o": ["(a + b)(a − b)", "(a − b)²", "(a + b)²", "a(a − b²)"], "e": "ab and −ab cancel when you multiply the brackets out."}
]},
{"q": [
{"t": "Factorise: x³ − 8", "o": ["(x − 2)(x² + 2x + 4)", "(x − 2)(x² − 2x + 4)", "(x − 2)³", "(x + 2)(x² − 2x + 4)"], "e": "a³ − b³ = (a − b)(a² + ab + b²) with b = 2."},
{"t": "Factorise: 6x² + 5x − 6", "o": ["(2x + 3)(3x − 2)", "(2x − 3)(3x + 2)", "(6x − 1)(x + 6)", "(3x + 3)(2x − 2)"], "e": "Product −36 and sum 5: 9 and −4. 6x² + 9x − 4x − 6 = 3x(2x + 3) − 2(2x + 3)."},
{"t": "Factorise: x³ + 27", "o": ["(x + 3)(x² − 3x + 9)", "(x + 3)(x² + 3x + 9)", "(x + 3)³", "(x − 3)(x² + 3x + 9)"], "e": "a³ + b³ = (a + b)(a² − ab + b²) with b = 3."},
{"t": "Use an identity to find 99³.", "n": 970299, "k": "99**3", "e": "(100 − 1)³ = 1000000 − 30000 + 300 − 1."},
{"t": "(x + y + z)² equals:", "o": ["x² + y² + z² + 2xy + 2yz + 2zx", "x² + y² + z²", "x² + y² + z² + xy + yz + zx", "x² + y² + z² + 2xyz"], "e": "Every term multiplies every other: three squares and each pair twice."},
{"t": "Factorise: 2x² − 7x + 3", "o": ["(2x − 1)(x − 3)", "(2x − 3)(x − 1)", "(2x + 1)(x − 3)", "(x − 1)(x − 3)"], "e": "Product 6 and sum −7: −6 and −1. 2x² − 6x − x + 3 = 2x(x − 3) − 1(x − 3)."},
{"t": "a³ − b³ equals:", "o": ["(a − b)(a² + ab + b²)", "(a − b)(a² − ab + b²)", "(a − b)³", "(a + b)(a² − ab + b²)"], "e": "The signs follow the pattern: same sign as the cubes in the first bracket, opposite in the middle of the second."},
{"t": "Factorise completely: x⁴ − 1", "o": ["(x² + 1)(x + 1)(x − 1)", "(x² + 1)(x² − 1)", "(x − 1)⁴", "(x + 1)²(x − 1)²"], "e": "(x²)² − 1 = (x² + 1)(x² − 1), and x² − 1 factorises again."},
{"t": "Use an identity to find 104 × 96.", "n": 9984, "k": "104*96", "e": "(100 + 4)(100 − 4) = 10000 − 16."},
{"t": "Factorise: x² + 1/x² + 2", "o": ["(x + 1/x)²", "(x − 1/x)²", "(x + 1/x)(x − 1/x)", "(x² + 1)²"], "e": "2 = 2 × x × (1/x), so this is a perfect square."}
]},
{"q": [
{"t": "Factorise: x³ − 23x² + 142x − 120", "o": ["(x − 1)(x − 10)(x − 12)", "(x − 2)(x − 6)(x − 10)", "(x − 1)(x − 8)(x − 15)", "(x + 1)(x − 10)(x − 12)"], "e": "p(1) = 1 − 23 + 142 − 120 = 0, so (x − 1) is a factor. Dividing leaves x² − 22x + 120 = (x − 10)(x − 12)."},
{"t": "If a + b + c = 0, then a³ + b³ + c³ equals:", "o": ["3abc", "0", "abc", "a² + b² + c²"], "e": "a³ + b³ + c³ − 3abc = (a + b + c)(…). If a + b + c = 0 the right side is 0."},
{"t": "Find (−12)³ + 7³ + 5³ without cubing.", "n": -1260, "k": "(-12)**3+7**3+5**3", "e": "−12 + 7 + 5 = 0, so the sum of cubes is 3 × (−12) × 7 × 5 = −1260."},
{"t": "If x + y = 5 and xy = 6, find x³ + y³.", "n": 35, "k": "5**3-3*6*5", "e": "x³ + y³ = (x + y)³ − 3xy(x + y) = 125 − 90."},
{"t": "Factorise: 8x³ + 27y³ + 36x²y + 54xy²", "o": ["(2x + 3y)³", "(2x − 3y)³", "(2x + 3y)(4x² + 9y²)", "(8x + 27y)³"], "e": "(2x)³ + (3y)³ + 3(2x)²(3y) + 3(2x)(3y)² matches (a + b)³."},
{"t": "Factorise: x³ − 3x² − 9x − 5", "o": ["(x + 1)²(x − 5)", "(x − 1)²(x + 5)", "(x + 1)(x − 1)(x − 5)", "(x + 1)(x + 5)(x − 1)"], "e": "p(−1) = −1 − 3 + 9 − 5 = 0. Dividing by (x + 1) leaves x² − 4x − 5 = (x + 1)(x − 5)."},
{"t": "Factorise: 27 − 125a³ − 135a + 225a²", "o": ["(3 − 5a)³", "(3 + 5a)³", "(5a − 3)³", "(3 − 5a)(9 + 25a²)"], "e": "3³ − 3(3)²(5a) + 3(3)(5a)² − (5a)³ matches (a − b)³."},
{"t": "If a − b = 4 and ab = 5, find a³ − b³.", "n": 124, "k": "4**3+3*5*4", "e": "a³ − b³ = (a − b)³ + 3ab(a − b) = 64 + 60."},
{"t": "Factorise: 4x² + y² + z² − 4xy − 2yz + 4xz", "o": ["(2x − y + z)²", "(2x + y + z)²", "(2x − y − z)²", "(2x + y − z)²"], "e": "Signs of the product terms: xy negative, yz negative, xz positive — so y has the opposite sign to x and z."},
{"t": "Find 28³ + (−15)³ + (−13)³ without cubing.", "n": 16380, "k": "28**3-15**3-13**3", "e": "28 − 15 − 13 = 0, so the sum is 3 × 28 × (−15) × (−13) = 16380."}
]},
{"q": [
{"t": "If x + 1/x = 3, find x³ + 1/x³.", "n": 18, "k": "3**3-3*3", "e": "(x + 1/x)³ = x³ + 1/x³ + 3(x + 1/x). So 27 − 9 = 18."},
{"t": "If a + b + c = 9 and ab + bc + ca = 26, find a³ + b³ + c³ − 3abc.", "n": 27, "k": "9*((81-52)-26)", "e": "a² + b² + c² = 81 − 52 = 29. The identity gives (a + b + c)(a² + b² + c² − ab − bc − ca) = 9 × 3."},
{"t": "If a² + b² + c² = ab + bc + ca for real numbers a, b, c, then:", "o": ["a = b = c", "a + b + c = 0", "abc = 0", "a = −b"], "e": "Doubling and rearranging gives (a − b)² + (b − c)² + (c − a)² = 0. Squares cannot be negative, so each is 0."},
{"t": "Factorise completely: x⁶ − y⁶", "o": ["(x − y)(x + y)(x² + xy + y²)(x² − xy + y²)", "(x³ − y³)²", "(x² − y²)³", "(x − y)⁶"], "e": "(x³)² − (y³)² = (x³ − y³)(x³ + y³), and each cube factorises again."},
{"t": "(x − y)³ + (y − z)³ + (z − x)³ equals:", "o": ["3(x − y)(y − z)(z − x)", "0", "(x − y)(y − z)(z − x)", "3xyz"], "e": "The three brackets add up to 0, so the sum of their cubes is 3 times their product."},
{"t": "If x² + 1/x² = 34 and x is positive, find x³ + 1/x³.", "n": 198, "k": "6**3-3*6", "e": "(x + 1/x)² = 36, so x + 1/x = 6. Then 216 − 18 = 198."},
{"t": "If x − 1/x = 2, find x³ − 1/x³.", "n": 14, "k": "2**3+3*2", "e": "(x − 1/x)³ = x³ − 1/x³ − 3(x − 1/x). So 8 + 6 = 14."},
{"t": "Factorise: x⁴ + 4", "o": ["(x² + 2x + 2)(x² − 2x + 2)", "(x² + 2)²", "(x² + 2)(x² − 2)", "It has no factors with whole-number coefficients"], "e": "Add and subtract 4x²: (x² + 2)² − (2x)², a difference of squares."},
{"t": "If a + b = 10 and a² + b² = 58, find a³ + b³.", "n": 370, "k": "10**3-3*21*10", "e": "2ab = 100 − 58, so ab = 21. Then 1000 − 3 × 21 × 10 = 370."},
{"t": "Factorise: 3x³ − x² − 3x + 1", "o": ["(3x − 1)(x + 1)(x − 1)", "(3x + 1)(x + 1)(x − 1)", "(3x − 1)(x − 1)²", "(x − 3)(x + 1)(x − 1)"], "e": "Group: x²(3x − 1) − 1(3x − 1) = (3x − 1)(x² − 1)."}
]}
]
}
